% hoamaint.zed -- Z rendering of SCORE HOA within-basin maintenance.
%
% PILOT EVIDENCE (2026-07-24) for the vault-formality question, which was
% declined: Z as a broad vault formality does not enter SCORE. Kept as that
% pilot's evidence artifact. NOTE: the Z track itself went LIVE the same
% day via a different door -- the refinement calculus (hoarefine.zed,
% formal/z/README.md, obsidian/SCORE/methodology/RefinementCalculus.md).
% Mirrors, name for name:
%   - Lean : formal/Formal/Score/HOAMaintenance.lean (\S{}HM1-HM8)
%   - TLA+ : formal/tla/HOA.tla
%   - vault: obsidian/SCORE/emergence/mechanism/HOA.md, Hysteresis.md
%
% Type-check (CZT toolchain lives in protocol-formal-template/z):
%   & ~\Dev\protocol-formal-template\z\run-czt.ps1 -File .\hoamaint.zed
%
% [IDIOM A] state schema, [IDIOM B] init, [IDIOM C] guarded ops,
% [IDIOM D] safety as horizontal schema -- per protocol-formal-template/z.

\section{hoamaint parents standard\_toolkit}

Hysteresis constants (Lean \S{}HM4: additive combine; HysteresisGap
assumption of HOA.tla).

\begin{axdef}
  maxlvl : \nat \\
  formation : \nat \\
  dissolution : \nat
\where
  0 < dissolution \\
  dissolution < formation \\
  formation - dissolution \leq maxlvl \\
  formation \leq 2 * maxlvl
\end{axdef}

\begin{zed}
  engagement == formation - dissolution
\end{zed}

\subsection{State [IDIOM A]}

HOAState: substrate + loop endowment, discretized to levels 0..maxlvl.

\begin{schema}{HOAState}
  substrate : \nat \\
  endowment : \nat
\where
  substrate \leq maxlvl \\
  endowment \leq maxlvl
\end{schema}

Characteristic subsets of state space, as horizontal schemas
(\S{}HM5-HM6: HOAExists, Basin, feedbackEngaged).

\begin{zed}
  HOAExists == [ HOAState | substrate + endowment \geq formation ]
\end{zed}

\begin{zed}
  Basin == [ HOAState | substrate \geq dissolution ]
\end{zed}

\begin{zed}
  Engaged == [ HOAState | endowment \geq engagement ]
\end{zed}

\subsection{Initial state [IDIOM B]}

Premise of MaintainedWithinIfPreserved: an existing HOA, in basin.

\begin{schema}{InitMaint}
  HOAExists \\
  Basin
\end{schema}

\subsection{Micro-moves [IDIOM C]}

The abstract HOAMove (\S{}HM6) made concrete: one micro-step moves
substrate or endowment by one level, within bounds (bounds enforced by
the primed state invariant).

\begin{schema}{SubUp}
  \Delta HOAState
\where
  substrate' = substrate + 1 \\
  endowment' = endowment
\end{schema}

\begin{schema}{SubDown}
  \Delta HOAState
\where
  1 \leq substrate \\
  substrate' = substrate - 1 \\
  endowment' = endowment
\end{schema}

\begin{schema}{EndUp}
  \Delta HOAState
\where
  endowment' = endowment + 1 \\
  substrate' = substrate
\end{schema}

\begin{schema}{EndDown}
  \Delta HOAState
\where
  1 \leq endowment \\
  endowment' = endowment - 1 \\
  substrate' = substrate
\end{schema}

\begin{zed}
  Move == SubUp \lor SubDown \lor EndUp \lor EndDown
\end{zed}

Basin-preserving, feedback-engaged move (the \S{}HM8 premise), by schema
conjunction over the generic Move:

\begin{zed}
  MaintMove == [ Move | substrate' \geq dissolution \land endowment' \geq engagement ]
\end{zed}

\subsection{Safety [IDIOM D]}

Maintenance: the HOA continues to exist. The \S{}HM8 claim is that
MaintMove preserves membership in this schema.

\begin{schema}{Maintenance}
  HOAState
\where
  substrate + endowment \geq formation
\end{schema}

The closes\_hysteresis\_gap proof obligation (discharged in Lean, not
here -- CZT typechecks it; Lean proves it):

\begin{zed}
  \vdash? \forall HOAState | substrate \geq dissolution \land endowment \geq engagement \spot substrate + endowment \geq formation
\end{zed}
